Validate choice shapes, null/empty rules, duplicates, missing and ambiguous lookups without raw Python/ORM errors. Use configured-key dictionaries with id fallback for single and multiple choices; the configured key wins when both occur. Preserve typed scalar lookups, return ordering, and falsy scalar/list defaults; reject structured lookup values.
Reject invalid configured defaults in model/admin validation; runtime serializers safely log and omit invalid defaults without rejecting explicit valid values or leaking bad defaults through metadata.
Validate defaults against surviving persisted inline choices, retain strict validation when no inline runs, reuse metadata choice queries, and ship German/French validation catalogs.
Apply configured custom-field defaults only on creation; omitted full-update fields preserve stored values and choice relations.
Prefetch choice catalogs only for input validation, including nested and list serializers; read serializers load field definitions without fetching unused choices.
Return fresh plain lists for multiple-choice input and defaults in catalog order without constructing QuerySets or modifying their private caches; remove the unused ChoiceIdField.get_queryset method.
